st-job-name-clf-survivor-coordinator = CLF Coordinator
st-job-prefix-clf-survivor-coordinator = CRDN
st-job-name-clf-survivor-synth = CLF Synthetic
st-job-prefix-clf-survivor-synth = Syn

st-job-greeting-clf-survivor = You are a member of the Colonial Liberation Front.

  You are NOT aware of the marines or their intentions.

  You are [bold][color=#ce1e1e][font size=16]HOSTILE to the UNMC![/font][/color][/bold]

st-clf-survivor-story-clf_ship = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a crash landing![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Your ship received a distress signal from a planet bordering CLF-controlled space under UNMC control. Ready and willing to save poor colonists from parasitic tyrants, you and your team boarded a small ship called Marie Curie. Unfortunately, right before you reached the landing zone, a glob of acid hit the ship, damaging one of the engines. Despite all the efforts of the pilot, the ship went straight into a nearby mountain. You were hurt pretty badly in the crash, but luckily none of your team were seriously hurt.

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfmining = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a colonial uprising![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Your cell has been embedded among the miners and workers of Solaris Ridge, instigating and agitating for a general strike. Your work was successful and the strike turned violent against UA peacekeeping forces. Soon after, in the chaos, you received word that unknown creatures were picking off fellow colonists. You hunkered down with your cell and began to prepare for the worst, not knowing what fate awaits you in these caves...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clf_pods = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a crash landing![/font][/bold]

  You are aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Your ship, due to poor maintenance, suffered a complete system failure and had to be abandoned. Your pods catastrophically failed, and you landed on the nearest planet. At first the colony appeared mostly abandoned, save for a company rat you found hiding in a supply locker. After some enhanced interrogation, you learned there has been an outbreak of dangerous creatures. Your cell hunkered down and repelled a wave of the creatures, suffering many casualties. You hang by a thread, stuck on an unknown world surrounded by unknown enemies.

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-rocinante_clf = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of an attempted prison break![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. You discovered that one of your comrades is being held temporarily at the Science Annex of the infamous Fiorina Prison. The plan was simple: ram your ship straight into the station and shoot your way through, relying on the element of surprise. However, station security was already on high alert and responded quickly. You beat them back, but now it is quiet... too quiet...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfraid_shivas = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a CLF raid![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. After a rough landing that disabled your strike craft, your cell successfully launched a raid against the corporate parasitic scum lording over this colony. However, the expected response from security forces never arrived, and the colony soon fell silent. Strange noises have been heard coming from the darkness, and the cell lead has ordered everyone to hold here until further orders.

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfsmugglers = [bold][font size=14]You are a CLF member running a smuggling operation![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. You and the rest of your team have been smuggling in this sector for years. After nearly running out of fuel running from a patrol, you barely managed to coast to a stop at the usual pickup zone at the refinery. However, the crew that usually meets you was nowhere to be found, and the colony was dead silent. You started moving cargo as usual and set up a perimeter just in case. Now, after dark, you have started hearing strange noises coming from the colony...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfcamp = [bold][font size=14]You are a CLF member in a covert camp![/font][/bold]

  You are aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Your cell has been training and negotiating for more equipment with the SPP for a few weeks now. Recently some sort of dangerous creatures invaded the nearby colony, and the radios fell silent. The creatures then attacked your encampment, causing multiple casualties. Your cell lead has requested extraction from HQ, hopefully they arrive in time...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfraid_varadero = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a crash landing![/font][/bold]

  You are aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Your cell was en route to a UA outpost when your shuttle suffered a critical systems failure and crashed. Almost immediately you were beset upon by unknown hostile creatures, which your team barely managed to beat back, not without serious losses. Defenses are prepared for the second assault, but you do not know how much longer you can hold out...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.

st-clf-survivor-story-clfspaceport = [bold][font size=14]You are a survivor of a CLF raid![/font][/bold]

  You are NOT aware of the xenomorph threat.

  You are fighting for the Colonial Liberation Front. Taking advantage of the chaos after most security forces in the city were diverted to the lab, your cell launched an assault on the nearby offices, knowing a company big shot would be present. The raid was a success with minimal losses, but the expected security response never arrived. In fact, the whole city seems to have gone quiet...

  Your primary objective is to [color=#ce1e1e]heal up and survive[/color]. You may not assault the hive on your own initiative, but you may defend yourself against the xenomorphs.
